---
import OnePage from '../layouts/OnePage.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { brand } from '../data/brand';

const domainDisplay = brand.url.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');

const title = `Privacy Policy | ${brand.name}`;
const description = `How ${brand.name} and ${brand.company.name} collect, use, disclose, retain and protect personal data through this website.`;
---

<OnePage title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <section class="legal" aria-labelledby="privacy-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 id="privacy-h">Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Ella Siew and {brand.company.name} (together, "we",
        "us" or "our") collect, use, disclose, retain and protect personal data through{' '}
        {domainDisplay} (the "Website"), our communications, consultations, content, products
        and services.
      </p>

      <p>
        The Website is the personal website of Ella Siew, jointly operated by Ella Siew and{' '}
        {brand.company.name}. The Website presents Ella Siew's personal brand, professional
        insights and services and connects visitors with services offered through{' '}
        {brand.company.name}. Ella Siew and {brand.company.name} jointly operate the Website and
        are responsible for the personal data described in this Policy. Unless a checkout page,
        proposal or service agreement expressly states otherwise, {brand.company.name} is the
        contracting service provider for paid services purchased through or following use of the
        Website.
      </p>

      <p>
        For the purposes of the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (Cap. 486) of Hong Kong (the
        "PDPO"), we act as data users in relation to personal data under our control. Where
        another applicable law uses the term "controller", we act as controllers unless a service
        agreement states that we process data only on a client's instructions.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This Policy applies to Website visitors, subscribers, prospective clients, clients,
        purchasers, people who book consultations, and business contacts. It covers interactions
        through the Website, Cal.com, email, telephone, newsletters, online checkout and related
        communications.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party websites and services have their own privacy practices. This Policy does not
        control how an independent third party processes data after you follow an external link
        or use its service.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Personal data we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Identity and contact data:</strong> name, email address, telephone number, company, job title, country or location, and preferred contact method.</li>
        <li><strong>Enquiry and booking data:</strong> messages, appointment time, time zone, meeting details, answers to booking questions, rescheduling or cancellation information, and information submitted through Website forms or Cal.com.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional and profile data:</strong> organisation, industry, role, website, LinkedIn or other public professional profile, expertise, audience, business objectives, brand positioning, marketing activities and project requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Service and correspondence data:</strong> proposals, contracts, instructions, call notes, feedback, deliverables, support requests and records of our communications.</li>
        <li><strong>Transaction and billing data:</strong> billing name and address, purchased item or service, amount, currency, tax information, payment status, transaction reference, invoice details and limited payment information supplied by a payment processor. We do not intend to store complete payment-card numbers or security codes.</li>
        <li><strong>Subscription and marketing data:</strong> newsletter registration, topics of interest, consent records, communication preferences, email engagement where enabled, and unsubscribe or objection requests.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical and usage data:</strong> IP address, browser and device information, operating system, referring page, pages viewed, dates and times, approximate location, cookie or similar identifiers, consent choices, server logs and security events.</li>
        <li><strong>Content you provide:</strong> documents, images, comments, survey answers, testimonials or other materials voluntarily supplied to us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Please do not provide sensitive personal data unless we specifically request it and explain why it is needed.</p>

      <h2>3. How we collect personal data</h2>
      <p>We collect personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>directly from you when you submit a form, book a consultation, subscribe, contact us, buy a product or service, sign an agreement or communicate with us;</li>
        <li>automatically through cookies, server logs and similar technologies when you use the Website;</li>
        <li>from service providers supporting scheduling, communications, payments, website operations and analytics;</li>
        <li>from public professional sources, such as a company website or LinkedIn profile, where relevant to an enquiry or business relationship; and</li>
        <li>from a colleague, employer, referrer or business partner where they introduce you or provide your business contact details lawfully.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you provide personal data about another person, you should have authority to do so and make this Policy available to that person where appropriate.</p>

      <h2>4. Why we use personal data</h2>
      <p>We may use personal data to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>respond to enquiries and communicate with you;</li>
        <li>arrange, manage and follow up consultations through Cal.com or other confirmed scheduling tools;</li>
        <li>assess your needs, prepare proposals and enter into contracts;</li>
        <li>provide personal-branding, AI visibility, AI SEO/GEO, advisory, content, digital product or other purchased services;</li>
        <li>create and administer accounts, orders, payments, invoices, refunds and transaction records;</li>
        <li>deliver newsletters, insights and offers where we have the required consent or other lawful permission;</li>
        <li>personalise content and understand how visitors use the Website;</li>
        <li>measure Website and campaign performance where analytics is enabled;</li>
        <li>secure, maintain, troubleshoot and improve the Website and our operations;</li>
        <li>detect fraud, misuse, security incidents and violations of our terms;</li>
        <li>establish, exercise or defend legal claims; and</li>
        <li>comply with legal, regulatory, tax, accounting and record-keeping duties.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We will not use personal data for a new purpose that is incompatible with the purpose for which it was collected unless permitted by law or we obtain any consent required.</p>

      <h2>5. Direct marketing</h2>
      <p>
        We may use your name, email address, contact details, professional interests and service
        history to send information and offers concerning personal branding, AI visibility, AI
        SEO/GEO, professional content, events, digital products and related consulting services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where the PDPO requires consent, we will provide the required information and obtain your
        consent before using personal data for direct marketing. Marketing consent is optional
        and is separate from acceptance of this Policy or our Terms of Use. We will not provide
        your personal data to another person for that person's direct marketing without the
        consent required by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may unsubscribe at any time without charge by using the unsubscribe link in an email
        or contacting <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>. We may retain a minimal
        suppression record to honour your request.
      </p>
      <p>
        Service messages relating to a booking, order, contract, payment, security matter or
        requested service are not promotional communications and may continue where necessary.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        As of publication, this Website does not use analytics or marketing cookies, and no
        non-essential tracking is active. The Website may in future use:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Necessary technologies</strong> required for security, network delivery, forms, consent preferences and core Website functions;</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics technologies</strong> to understand traffic, page usage and performance; and</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing technologies</strong> to measure campaigns or personalise promotional activity, if introduced.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Where required, non-essential analytics or marketing technologies will operate only after
        you make the relevant consent choice, and a cookie banner or settings control will be
        added at that time. You may also restrict cookies through your browser, although doing so
        can affect Website functions.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not claim to use a provider that has not been implemented. This section will be
        updated to name the specific provider before it is switched on.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Payments</h2>
      <p>
        As of publication, this Website does not process online payments. If online payment is
        introduced, payments will be processed by an independent payment provider. That provider
        may collect payment-card, bank, authentication, fraud-prevention and transaction
        information under its own privacy notice. We would generally receive confirmation,
        transaction references and limited billing details rather than complete card credentials.
      </p>
      <p>
        The checkout page will identify the payment provider or provide access to its applicable
        terms and privacy information once a provider is confirmed. Transaction information would
        be used to process orders, deliver purchases, manage refunds or disputes, prevent fraud
        and meet accounting and legal duties.
      </p>

      <h2>8. How we disclose personal data</h2>
      <p>We may disclose relevant personal data to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>{brand.company.name} personnel, contractors and professional advisers who need it for authorised work;</li>
        <li><strong>Cal.com, Inc.</strong>, which we use for appointment scheduling (<a href="https://cal.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cal.com/privacy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>);</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>, which we use for website hosting and content delivery (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>);</li>
        <li><strong>Google LLC</strong>, which we use for website typography via Google Fonts (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>);</li>
        <li>email, newsletter, customer-relationship, communications, payment and analytics providers, if and when we engage one;</li>
        <li>a purchaser, investor or adviser involved in a genuine corporate transaction, subject to appropriate safeguards;</li>
        <li>regulators, courts, law-enforcement agencies or other persons where disclosure is required or permitted by law; and</li>
        <li>other persons with your direction or consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Service providers are expected to handle personal data only for authorised purposes and with appropriate protection. We do not sell personal data.</p>

      <h2>9. International processing</h2>
      <p>
        We are based in Hong Kong and serve an international audience. Service providers may
        store or process personal data in Hong Kong or other jurisdictions, including Cal.com,
        Cloudflare and Google as named above. Privacy laws and enforcement may differ between
        locations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where required by applicable law, we use contractual or other appropriate safeguards for
        cross-border processing. By using an external service such as Cal.com or a payment
        provider, your data may also be processed in locations described in that provider's
        privacy notice.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes
        described in this Policy, including to provide services, maintain business and
        transaction records, honour marketing objections, resolve disputes and comply with legal,
        tax and accounting requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Retention periods vary according to the type of record, the relationship, legal
        obligations and the risk involved. When personal data is no longer required, we will
        delete, anonymise or securely dispose of it, subject to lawful backup and archival
        cycles.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical and organisational measures designed to
        protect personal data against unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure, loss or
        misuse. These may include access controls, secure service providers, encryption in
        transit, authentication, backups and operational controls.
      </p>
      <p>
        No internet transmission or storage system is completely secure. You are responsible for
        protecting your own account credentials, devices and copies of communications.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable law, you may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request access to personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>request correction of inaccurate personal data;</li>
        <li>withdraw a consent where processing depends on consent, without affecting earlier lawful processing;</li>
        <li>object to or opt out of direct marketing;</li>
        <li>request deletion, restriction, portability or objection where another applicable privacy law grants those rights; and</li>
        <li>complain to an applicable privacy regulator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a> with the
        subject "Privacy Request" and describe the relevant records. We may need to verify your
        identity. Requests under the PDPO will be handled in accordance with its requirements,
        including any lawful fee or exception.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Website and our business services are intended for adults and are not directed to
        children. We do not knowingly seek personal data from children. If you believe a child
        has provided personal data without appropriate authority, contact us so we can assess and
        address it.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Third-party links and embedded services</h2>
      <p>
        The Website may link to or embed services such as Cal.com, social networks, video
        platforms or payment pages. Those services may collect data directly from you and operate
        under their own terms and privacy notices. Review those notices before providing
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Changes to this Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise this Policy when our practices, services, providers or legal obligations
        change. The current version will be posted on this page. If a change materially affects
        how we use personal data, we will provide additional notice or seek consent where
        required.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Contact</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions, requests or complaints, contact:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Ella Siew and {brand.company.name}</strong><br />
        Website: {domainDisplay}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</OnePage>
